# Hideki testnet configuration (chain 50383). The read-only research path needs no private key.
# WALLET_ADDRESS is public; blank means hypothetical preflight analysis.
# CHAIN_ID labels the datasets this tool writes and caches. It cannot move a read: those go through
# the chain object in src/client.ts. If the two differ the interface says so instead of hiding it.
WALLET_ADDRESS=
CHAIN_ID=50383
RPC_URL=https://api.hideki2.infra.testnet.somnia.network
WS_URL=wss://api.hideki2.infra.testnet.somnia.network/ws
INDEXER_URL=https://hideki-dev.smk.somnia.host/v1/graphql

# How long a deployment may reuse the market list and a pool's live risk parameters, in seconds.
# Unset locally, which means every request re-reads the venue: a remembered imBps is a run priced by
# parameters the chain may no longer enforce. `api/[...all].ts` sets 60 for the deployment only.
# See src/data/live-cache.ts for why the failure of a read is never remembered.
# PERP_SIM_LIVE_CACHE_SEC=60

# Bounded execution (local-only, 2026-11-14). The public deployment configures NONE of these and
# refuses POST /api/execute regardless. Off and preview-only by default: a dry-run reads the live
# market and prints the exact calldata a live placement would broadcast, without a signer or a send.
# To place ONE real testnet order locally: fund the wallet (Hideki faucet), set EXECUTION_ENABLED=true
# and DRY_RUN=false, put your funded key in PRIVATE_KEY, then run `pnpm execute --live --confirm`
# (or tick the confirm in the local web panel). The key is read here but never logged, serialised
# into a response, or committed — .env is gitignored. EXECUTION_MAX_NOTIONAL caps one order's
# notional in quote units; the policy kernel refuses to send over it. See docs/execution.md.
EXECUTION_ENABLED=false
DRY_RUN=true
PRIVATE_KEY=
EXECUTION_MAX_NOTIONAL=100
